        ],
        "html_path": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14199298/observations/step-q143560-e9bc84a0142d5cc4ad7c.html",
        "screenshot": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14199298/observations/step-q143560-e9bc84a0142d5cc4ad7c.png",
        "worked_solution": "Let $M$ be the event that a person selected was a male, and\n\n- let ${A}_{1}$ be the event that the person was under $18$,\n\n- let ${A}_{2}$ be the event that the person was between $18$ and $40$, and\n\n- let ${A}_{3}$ be the event that the person was over $40.$\n\nThen the disjoint union ${A}_{1}⊔{A}_{2}⊔{A}_{3}$ covers the entire sample space.\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected person is male, we use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(M)=P(M\\cap {A}_{1})+P(M\\cap {A}_{2})+P(M\\cap {A}_{3})\n$$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\nP(M\\cap {A}_{1})=0.16,\\,P(M\\cap {A}_{2})=0.3\\,P(M\\cap {A}_{3})=0.24.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the above information into the law of total probability, the probability that a randomly selected person is male is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(M) & =P(M\\cap {A}_{1})+P(M\\cap {A}_{2})+P(M\\cap {A}_{3}) \\\\  & =0.16+0.3+0.24 \\\\  & =0.7.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        "can_dont_know": false,
        "can_skip": false,
        "question": {
          "dom_id": "step-q143560",
          "name": "Question 1",
          "problem": "Among the people arrested in a particular city in 2010, $16%$ were males under $18,$ $30%$  were males between $18$ and $40,$ and $24%$ were males over $40.$ What is the probability that a person randomly selected from all those arrested in 2010 is male?",
          "worked_solution": "Let $M$ be the event that a person selected was a male, and\n\n- let ${A}_{1}$ be the event that the person was under $18$,\n\n- let ${A}_{2}$ be the event that the person was between $18$ and $40$, and\n\n- let ${A}_{3}$ be the event that the person was over $40.$\n\nThen the disjoint union ${A}_{1}⊔{A}_{2}⊔{A}_{3}$ covers the entire sample space.\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected person is male, we use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(M)=P(M\\cap {A}_{1})+P(M\\cap {A}_{2})+P(M\\cap {A}_{3})\n$$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\nP(M\\cap {A}_{1})=0.16,\\,P(M\\cap {A}_{2})=0.3\\,P(M\\cap {A}_{3})=0.24.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the above information into the law of total probability, the probability that a randomly selected person is male is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(M) & =P(M\\cap {A}_{1})+P(M\\cap {A}_{2})+P(M\\cap {A}_{3}) \\\\  & =0.16+0.3+0.24 \\\\  & =0.7.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          "calculator_instructions": "",
          "fields": [
            {
              "key": "selection",
              "type": "radio",
              "choices": [
                {
                  "option": "a",
                  "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-143560-a",
                  "type": "math",
                  "value": "0.65",
                  "html": "<mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"16\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c30\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2E\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c36\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c35\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0.65</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>  "
                },
                {
