      "solution": {
        "status": "ambiguous",
        "reasoning": "Even distribution makes plant shares equal to area shares, so forest C contains 1−0.40−0.25=0.35 of the plants. Let x be its poisonous proportion. Then 0.24=0.40×0.30+0.25×0.20+0.35x=0.17+0.35x, giving x=0.07/0.35=0.20=20%, option a. No Math Academy answer or grade for this question is captured; the worked example concerns a different problem.",
        "confidence": 1,
        "answers": [
