        ],
        "html_path": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14199298/observations/step-q143902-d4b561952cb6b14fa2eb.html",
        "screenshot": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14199298/observations/step-q143902-d4b561952cb6b14fa2eb.png",
        "worked_solution": "Let $G$ be the event of selecting a green marble at random from one of the three bags, and \n\n- let $A$ be the event that the marble is from bag $A,$\n\n- let $B$ be the event that the marble is from bag $B,$\n\n- let $C$ be the event that the marble is from bag $C.$\n\nThen the disjoint union $A⊔B⊔C$ covers the entire sample space. \n\nTo calculate the probability of selecting a green marble, we can use the law of total probability: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(G) & =P(G\\cap A)+P(G\\cap B)+P(G\\cap C) \\\\  & =P(G|A)P(A)+P(G|B)P(B)+P(G|C)P(C)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each piece of information into mathematical notation.\n\n- Since a bag is selected at random, we have\n\n$$\nP(A)=P(B)=P(C)=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$\n\n- Since there are $8$ green marbles out of $20$  in bag $A,$ and  $6$ green marbles out of $20$  in bag $B,$ we have \n\n$$\nP(G|A)=\\frac{8}{20},\\,P(G|B)=\\frac{6}{20}.\n$$\n\n- Since the probability of picking a green marble  from one of the bags is $\\frac{2}{5},$ we have\n\n$$\nP(G)=\\frac{2}{5}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability and solving for $P(G|C),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(G) & =P(G|A)P(A)+P(G|B)P(B)+P(G|C)P(C) \\\\ \\frac{2}{5} & =(\\frac{8}{20})(\\frac{1}{3})+(\\frac{6}{20})(\\frac{1}{3})+P(G|C)(\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\ \\frac{2}{5} & =\\frac{2}{15}+\\frac{1}{10}+(\\frac{1}{3})P(G|C) \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot P(G|C) & =\\frac{2}{5}-\\frac{2}{15}-\\frac{1}{10} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot P(G|C) & =\\frac{1}{6} \\\\ P(G|C) & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{1}{2}$ of the marbles from bag $C$ are green.",
        "can_dont_know": false,
        "can_skip": false,
        "question": {
          "dom_id": "step-q143902",
          "name": "Question 15",
          "problem": "Three bags, $A,B,$ and $C,$ contain marbles. Bag $A$ contains $12$ red and $8$ green marbles, while bag $B$ contains $14$ red and $6$ green marbles. A bag is selected at random, and a marble is randomly selected from the bag. If the probability that the selected marble is green is $\\frac{2}{5},$  what proportion of marbles from bag $C$ are green?",
          "worked_solution": "Let $G$ be the event of selecting a green marble at random from one of the three bags, and \n\n- let $A$ be the event that the marble is from bag $A,$\n\n- let $B$ be the event that the marble is from bag $B,$\n\n- let $C$ be the event that the marble is from bag $C.$\n\nThen the disjoint union $A⊔B⊔C$ covers the entire sample space. \n\nTo calculate the probability of selecting a green marble, we can use the law of total probability: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(G) & =P(G\\cap A)+P(G\\cap B)+P(G\\cap C) \\\\  & =P(G|A)P(A)+P(G|B)P(B)+P(G|C)P(C)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each piece of information into mathematical notation.\n\n- Since a bag is selected at random, we have\n\n$$\nP(A)=P(B)=P(C)=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$\n\n- Since there are $8$ green marbles out of $20$  in bag $A,$ and  $6$ green marbles out of $20$  in bag $B,$ we have \n\n$$\nP(G|A)=\\frac{8}{20},\\,P(G|B)=\\frac{6}{20}.\n$$\n\n- Since the probability of picking a green marble  from one of the bags is $\\frac{2}{5},$ we have\n\n$$\nP(G)=\\frac{2}{5}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability and solving for $P(G|C),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(G) & =P(G|A)P(A)+P(G|B)P(B)+P(G|C)P(C) \\\\ \\frac{2}{5} & =(\\frac{8}{20})(\\frac{1}{3})+(\\frac{6}{20})(\\frac{1}{3})+P(G|C)(\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\ \\frac{2}{5} & =\\frac{2}{15}+\\frac{1}{10}+(\\frac{1}{3})P(G|C) \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot P(G|C) & =\\frac{2}{5}-\\frac{2}{15}-\\frac{1}{10} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot P(G|C) & =\\frac{1}{6} \\\\ P(G|C) & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{1}{2}$ of the marbles from bag $C$ are green.",
          "calculator_instructions": "",
          "fields": [
            {
              "key": "selection",
              "type": "radio",
              "choices": [
                {
                  "option": "a",
                  "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-143902-a",
                  "type": "math",
                  "value": "\\frac{4}{5}",
                  "html": "<mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"511\" style=\"font-size: 119.6%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mstyle><mjx-mfrac><mjx-frac type=\"d\"><mjx-num><mjx-nstrut type=\"d\"></mjx-nstrut><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c34\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-num><mjx-dbox><mjx-dtable><mjx-line type=\"d\"></mjx-line><mjx-row><mjx-den><mjx-dstrut type=\"d\"></mjx-dstrut><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c35\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-den></mjx-row></mjx-dtable></mjx-dbox></mjx-frac></mjx-mfrac></mjx-mstyle></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></mstyle></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>"
                },
                {
                  "option": "b",
                  "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-143902-b",
                  "type": "math",
                  "value": "\\frac{1}{2}",
                  "html": "<mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"512\" style=\"font-size: 119.6%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mstyle><mjx-mfrac><mjx-frac type=\"d\"><mjx-num><mjx-nstrut type=\"d\"></mjx-nstrut><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-num><mjx-dbox><mjx-dtable><mjx-line type=\"d\"></mjx-line><mjx-row><mjx-den><mjx-dstrut type=\"d\"></mjx-dstrut><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c32\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-den></mjx-row></mjx-dtable></mjx-dbox></mjx-frac></mjx-mfrac></mjx-mstyle></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>"
                },
                {
                  "option": "c",
                  "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-143902-c",
