      {
        "dom_id": "question-143723",
        "name": null,
        "problem": "Among all the people that visited Bill's ice cream shop last weekend, $25%$ were females under $18,$ $20%$ were females between $18$ and $30,$ and $15%$ were females over $30.$ What is the probability that a randomly selected person who visited Bill's shop last weekend is female?",
        "worked_solution": "Let $F$ be the event that a person selected was a female.\n\n- let ${A}_{1}$ be the event that the person was under $18$,\n\n- let ${A}_{2}$ be the event that the person was at least  $18$ but under $30$,\n\n- let ${A}_{3}$ be the event that the person was at least $30$ or older.\n\nThen the disjoint union ${A}_{1}⊔{A}_{2}⊔{A}_{3}$ covers the entire sample space.\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected person was a female, we use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(F)=P(F\\cap {A}_{1})+P(F\\cap {A}_{2})+P(F\\cap {A}_{3})\n$$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\nP(F\\cap {A}_{1})=0.25,\\,P(F\\cap {A}_{2})=0.2\\,P(F\\cap {A}_{3})=0.15.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the above information into the law of total probability, the probability that a randomly selected person is a female is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(F) & =P(F\\cap {A}_{1})+P(F\\cap {A}_{2})+P(F\\cap {A}_{3}) \\\\  & =0.25+0.2+0.15 \\\\  & =0.6.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        "calculator_instructions": "",
        "fields": [],
        "problem_field_keys": [],
        "answer_fields_complete": null,
        "result": "Correct",
        "proof_feedback": null,
        "html": "<div id=\"question-143723\" class=\"question\"><div class=\"questionHeader\"><span class=\"questionNumber\">5.</span><span class=\"helpButton\" questionid=\"143723\">?</span></div><div class=\"questionText\"><p>Among all the people that visited Bill's ice cream shop last weekend, <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"112\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c32\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c35\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c25\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">%</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> were females under <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"113\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c38\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2C\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>18</mn><mo>,</mo></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"114\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c32\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c30\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c25\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">%</mi></math></mjx-ass