4 56T220 -22Q138 -22 78 21T18 123Q18 184 61 227T156 274Q178 274 178 263Q178 260 177 258Q172 247 164 239T151 227T136 218L127 213L124 202Q118 186 118 163Q120 124 165 86T292 48Q374 48 423 86T473 186V193Q473 267 347 327Q268 364 239 389Q191 431 191 486Q191 547 242 600T356 679T470 705Q472 705 478 705T489 704Q551 704 596 682T642 610Q642 566 621 545Q592 516 554 512Z\" id=\"E18-MJCAL-53\" stroke-width=\"1\"></path>\n</defs>\n<g aria-hidden=\"true\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)\">\n<use x=\"0\" xlink:href=\"#E18-MJCAL-53\" y=\"0\"></use>\n</g>\n</svg></span> consisting of three events. However, it should be noted that the law of total probability can be extended to an arbitrary number of events, that is</p>\n<p><span class=\"mjpage mjpage__block\"><svg aria-labelledby=\"MathJax-SVG-19-Title\" focusable=\"false\" height=\"9.843ex\" role=\"img\" style=\"vertical-align: -4.06ex; margin-bottom: -0.278ex;\" viewbox=\"0 -2370 16769.7 4237.8\" width=\"38.949ex\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">\n<title id=\"MathJax-SVG-19-Title\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"2\" display=\"true\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\"><mjx-math aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"MJX-TEX\" display=\"true\" style=\"margin-left: 0px; margin-right: 0px;\"><mjx-mtable style=\"min-width: 16.401em;\"><mjx-table><mjx-itable><mjx-mtr><mjx-mtd style=\"text-align: right; padding-right: 0px; padding-bottom: 0.4em;\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D443 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c28\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D434 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c29\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-tstrut></mjx-tstrut></mjx-mtd><mjx-mtd style=\"text-align: left; padding-left: 0px; padding-bottom: 0.4em;\"><mjx-mi class=\"